  1. Root Cause: In macOS / SFML 3, when exiting via `exit()` or returning from `main()`, static destruction of `Game` singleton ran `sf::RenderWindow::~RenderWindow()` -> `sf::GlResource` -> `sf::priv::SFContext::~SFContext()` after macOS Cocoa / OpenGL windowing resources were already torn down by OS static teardown, causing `__abort_message` and `SIGABRT` (Abort trap 6).
  2. Resolution: Updated `Game::shutdown()` in `Game.cpp` to explicitly invoke `m_window.close()` during normal runtime shutdown, ensuring OpenGL contexts and window handles are destroyed cleanly while the windowing system is fully active. Updated `Game::quit()` to signal `m_isRunning = false` so control loops exit cleanly into `shutdown()`.
