- AUDIT (no code changes yet) of Camera, MapGenerator and Entities for gameplay completion. Key findings:
  * CAMERA: the reported out-of-bounds is real and has 4 independent causes. (1) All three sub-levels are 640px tall vs a 720px view; the clamp's else-branch locks Y to the map centre, so the view spans -40..680 — 40px of void above AND below. (2) Screen shake is added AFTER the clamp in Camera::update, so any shake escapes bounds on every map. (3) MapEditor calls setBoundsEnabled(false) on F1 and nothing ever re-enables it, so one editor visit unbounds the camera for the rest of the session. (4) Two sites write getView().setCenter() directly, bypassing the clamp; the void-fall one is then immediately overwritten by update() and is dead code.
  * CAMERA: main levels are 736px vs a 720px view = 16px of vertical pan, so the camera is effectively locked vertically and vertical level design is impossible.
  * GAMEPLAY: the game cannot be won. Flagpole publishes LevelComplete but the only subscribers are SoundManager and AchievementManager — nothing advances the level, loads the next map, or shows a victory screen.
  * GAMEPLAY: the level timer never counts down. m_levelTimer is set to 300, displayed in the HUD and snapshotted for rewind, but never decremented. No time pressure, no TimeWarning (never published despite a subscriber), no time-out death.
  * GAMEPLAY: checkpoints are not respawn points. Void-fall respawn is hardcoded to (96,64) regardless of level or progress; CheckpointActivated only triggers an autosave and is semantically overloaded (Pipe publishes it for warps).
  * GAMEPLAY: 6 EventTypes are declared and never published — TimeWarning, GameStart, StateChanged, PauseToggled, GroundPoundSlam, ScreenShakeTriggered. GroundPoundSlam has 2 subscribers (camera shake, SFX) so ground pound lands with no feedback.
  * MAPGEN: pit widths 2-4 tiles are inside the 3.5-tile walking jump, so generated levels are solvable — the guardrail works. The MovingPlatform mitigation is inert though (EntityFactory passes travelRange (0,0), audit B-5).
  * MAPGEN: default height 23 tiles = 736px reproduces the 16px-pan camera problem for generated levels too.
  * The two new -Wreorder-ctor warnings (MovingPlatform, HiddenBlock) were checked and are benign — the dependent member is declared before its dependency in both.
- No code changes made this session beyond the merge; findings reported to the user for prioritisation.
