- ROOT CAUSE of "Generate & Edit is not working": not the generator. enter()
  starts a 0.45s fade-in; render() draws that overlay after the world; the map
  editor branch of update() returned before ScreenTransitionManager::update(),
  so the fade sat at full black forever. The editor grid draws after the overlay
  — hence black screen WITH grid, exactly as reported.
- HOW IT WAS FOUND, and the method worth keeping: I built a throwaway harness
  that rendered the real PlayingState in Generate&Edit mode to an off-screen
  RenderTexture and printed a colour histogram. It came back with exactly two
  colours: #000000 and #2D2D2D. 0x2D is 45, and the editor grid is white at
  alpha 45 over black. That one number identified the entire remaining content
  of the frame as "the grid, over nothing" and pointed straight at an opaque
  overlay rather than a missing world. Speculating from the screenshot had me
  looking at the generator and the camera, both of which were fine.
- SECOND BUG, same report: MapGenerator's theme never reached BackgroundRenderer.
  Castle/ice/underground generated levels were drawn against the overworld blue
  sky and green hills. Both procedural paths (enter and regenerate) now set it.
- THIRD BUG, and the reason my earlier panel-layout work had no visible effect:
  a stale untracked imgui.ini at the repo root held Pos=60,60 for all six dev
  windows. ImGui's saved layout beats every ImGuiCond_FirstUseEver in the code,
  so the positions I set were being silently discarded on this machine. The ini
  filename is now versioned (imgui_layout_v2.ini) and the unversioned file is
  removed on startup, so a future default-layout change can retire the old file
  instead of fighting it. Worth remembering: ImGuiCond_FirstUseEver is not a
  default, it is a default *for a machine that has never run the program*.
