  code that does the removal, not by whoever happens to read it next.
- SHELL PICKUP: PhysicsEngine::update cleared the movement intent flags in the
  MIDDLE of update(), before the collision resolution at the END of the same
  update() read them. isRunRequested() was therefore always false by the time
  the resolver asked, so "hold run to carry" could never fire in the real game.
  My own regression test passed because it called the resolver directly with the
  flag freshly set — the same shape of mistake as the old fireball test. Fixed by
  clearing the flags at the end of update().
  LESSON: when a test drives one function directly, it is not testing the order
  the game calls things in. Drive the pipeline.
