  its anchor, i.e. sitting on the pipe mouth in full view. Now drawn clipped to
  the portion above the mouth, so it slides out, and non-collidable while inside.
- "MADNESS OF MUSIC": Pipe::checkWarp was declared const and played a sound,
  teleported the player and published an event. PlayingState called it once per
  pipe per frame, so holding crouch re-fired everything every frame. And the
  event it published was CheckpointActivated ("Warp event type mapping" in the
  comment) — so every warp also set a respawn point, ran an auto-save and played
  the checkpoint jingle. Two overlapping sounds a frame at 60Hz. checkWarp is a
  pure query now; added a real PlayerWarped event; added a 0.75s cooldown; and
  the level swap moved out of the loop over m_entities that it was replacing.
- "VOID BUT NOT DYING": three gaps. The void check only tested Y, so a player
  past the map edge never fell and never died. A pipe exit was trusted even when
  outside its destination. And a spawn point in the void respawned you into it
  repeatedly. All three closed, with a fallback to the level's own spawn point.
