- FIXED A REAL BUG the migration surfaced: EventBus::ScopedSubscription::~ScopedSubscription() calls EventBus::getInstance().unsubscribe(), and a std::vector<ScopedSubscription> owned by a Meyer's-singleton (AchievementManager, StatisticsTracker) destructs at static-destruction time. Function-local statics destruct in REVERSE order of first construction, and which of EventBus's-or-a-given-singleton's static is constructed first depends on which code path calls EventBus::getInstance() first at runtime (in this case, inside the singleton's own init()) — not something callers control. This meant EventBus's static instance could already be destroyed by the time a singleton's ScopedSubscriptions destructed, and calling EventBus::getInstance() again on a dead function-local static is undefined behaviour — observed as SIGSEGV. Fixed with a `bool g_eventBusAlive = true` (constant-initialized, so safe to read from any other destructor regardless of order) flipped false in a newly-added ~EventBus(), checked by ScopedSubscription::reset() before touching EventBus::getInstance().
