- Real reduction, stated honestly: disk 737M -> 384M (~48% smaller, not the ~90% a naive "133 sources x 25 targets -> x2" estimate would suggest) and object files 3443 -> 499 (~85% fewer). The gap between the two is because each of the 23+ linked executables still statically embeds the whole app's code and SFML/ImGui-SFML static libraries — object-file de-duplication doesn't shrink the executables themselves, and per-executable link size dominates build-tree disk once compilation is de-duplicated. Compile TIME reduction was not independently isolated this session (ccache, already configured in shared-build.cmake, was caching compiles across both the before- and after- builds, so a time comparison would conflate ccache hits with the object-library change); the object-file count and disk-size drop are the load-bearing measurements here.
- generate_game_levels was also converted to link AppObjectsRelease instead of naming APP_SOURCES itself — in scope as the same file, same mechanism, and it was a third independent full compile of the app that the object-library fix could remove for free.
- Dead code removed as part of the same edit: a stray `set(APP_SOURCES ${SOURCES}); list(REMOVE_ITEM ...)` reset before verify_minimap_visual, and the `list(FILTER SOURCES EXCLUDE REGEX ...)` line — both were vestiges of the old per-target-compiles-APP_SOURCES mechanism and did nothing once add_verify_test() stopped consuming ${APP_SOURCES} directly.
