- ONE ASSET TREE. tools/generate_game_levels.cpp wrote every level twice, once
  relative to cwd and once to "../", creating an untracked second tree at the
  repo root. ResourceManager::resolvePath tries the bare relative path FIRST, so
  which tree the game read depended on the launch directory. The root tree was
  raw generator output frozen nine minutes before 309c1a5 and cc6a32d fixed the
  very defects it still contained. Three separately-reported defects (half pipes,
  the 1-1 Sub spawn + P-Switch pit, "level detail is different") were ONE bug.
  Dual-write deleted, /assets/ gitignored, guard added and mutation-tested.
  The stray tree was backed up outside the repo before removal, per rule 7.
- PIPES: rendering now walks a run to both ends and pairs columns from its start;
  an unpaired column draws a complete narrow pipe, so a half is unrepresentable.
  MapGenerator still emitted a 1-column checkpoint pipe (cc6a32d fixed the same
  bug in generateSubLevel and missed this site). Warp pipes are 2x4 tiles.
  Pipe y moved by a measured rule, not a blanket -2: the foot sits one row into
  its floor so the rim is 3 tiles up, because JUMP_HEIGHT is exactly 4 tiles and
  a sub-level's exit pipe is the only way out of the room.
- SPAWNS: all three sub-levels spawned INSIDE their own entrance pipe; masked only
  because the warp override was valid. The guard could not catch it because it
  scanned downward FROM the spawn and hit that same pipe. Now rejects a spawn
  whose own box overlaps solid, and is wired into the flagpole/level-select path
  too, which had no guard at all.
- CASTLE: level_1 kept a legacy 5x5 fake-castle slab; the real castle settled on
  its roof, 5 tiles above its own flagpole, and the end-of-level walk drove the
  player into that slab's wall for three seconds. Slab deleted. The truncated
  castle_end sprite is already fixed on dev — shipping dev→main completes it.
- ENTITIES: platforms were double-integrated so tile push-out was overwritten
  every frame (and displacement was identically zero, meaning platforms have
  never carried the player); now kinematic with a shared terrain probe. Lakitu's
  3-spiny cap was a LIFETIME cap on a timer starting at level load 5500px away,
  so it spent every drop off-camera — now concurrent and engagement-gated.
  Bowser had no arena clamp where BoomBoom has one and his turnaround was dead
  code, so his phase-2 leap cleared the enclosure and softlocked the fight.
- UI: no text-fitting mechanism existed. Added fitCharSize/drawTextFitted/
  wrapText and gave drawMenuItems its panel's right edge. IMPORTANT FINDING:
  PressStart2P is NOT exactly monospace as assumed — the advance is hinted per
  size and size 12 lays out at 13px/char, so a closed-form budget overestimates
  by ~8% at exactly the size the LOAD GAME page uses. The verify-and-step-down
  loop is load-bearing, not defensive.
