  GameOverState>(summary))` with no `m_isPlaytest` check, unlike
  `leaveToCallingScreen()` and `advanceToNextLevel()`, which both already
  branch on it and `popState()` instead — so a playtest's last death replaced
  PlayingState with GameOverState (a GameStateManager `Change`, which only
  swaps the TOP of the stack) while the suspended EditorState stayed buried
  underneath, and GameOverState's own RETRY LEVEL / QUIT TO MENU choices
  (`changeState()` again) could only ever reach the main menu from there —
  never the editor.
