  consistent with it: `leaveToCallingScreen()` checks `m_isPlaytest` and
  calls `Game::popState()` instead of `changeState(MenuState)`, which is safe
  specifically because EditorState is the very next entry down the
  `GameStateManager` stack (pushed there by `EditorState::playtest()`) — a
  pop reveals it exactly as F5 left it, generically, via the existing
  deferred push/pop/change queue (no reaching around it). The fix threads
  `RunSummary::isPlaytest` from `m_isPlaytest` (new field, GameOverState.hpp;
  set in `PlayingState::buildRunSummary()`) so `GameOverState` can tell a
  playtest death from a real one, then makes its OWN dismissal path do the
  identical `Game::popState()` for that case — a new
