  `m_selected`) is the routing decision `activateSelection()` now switches on
  (RetryLevel / QuitToMenu / ReturnToEditor), and `handleInput()`'s Escape
  case checks the same flag directly (Escape's semantics — always quit,
  ignoring row selection — don't fit dismissAction()'s selection-aware
  contract, so it is not routed through it). The constructor also collapses
  the menu to a single "BACK TO EDITOR" item for a playtest run: RETRY LEVEL
